{"step_index":7579,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T17:27:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T17:27:55Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T17:27:57Z\nThe search for \"\"az restore-point create\" without consistency-mode site:learn.microsoft.com\" returned the following summary:\nWhen using the `az restore-point create` command in the Azure CLI, the `--consistency-mode` parameter is **optional**[1][2].\n\nIf you omit the `--consistency-mode` parameter, the operation will proceed using the default behavior[3]. Currently, **`CrashConsistent`** is the standard consistency mode used by default when no specific mode is provided[3][4].\n\n### Summary of Usage\n*   **Default Behavior:** If you run `az restore-point create --resource-group <rg> --collection-name <collection> --name <rp-name>`, it will default to `CrashConsistent`[1][2][3].\n*   **Explicit Usage:** You only need to include `--consistency-mode CrashConsistent` if you wish to explicitly define it in your script or command[1][5]. \n\nFor further details on restore points, you can refer to the official [Azure Restore Points documentation](https://aka.ms/RestorePoints)[6][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFVs0PA_c1HuLQV3jzixVkTNBxZC1sWYH_QWhYUaCRcC2jrQIW2_VSfD3N2qYBh7RE4sgajuHrfyXarauSCa57M1GCUHcTkDcoDZIfpuLnEd_ATgBuWCoeCz_TiJ5vAKabUFnFre_-viRFuuswqHBE2UOPzj3O0aD4AOw3LVeVdmNBPuQtkL6Dc4jP4JrckK9sHfM5KGrgfRHk=)\n[2] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFVs0PA_c1HuLQV3jzixVkTNBxZC1sWYH_QWhYUaCRcC2jrQIW2_VSfD3N2qYBh7RE4sgajuHrfyXarauSCa57M1GCUHcTkDcoDZIfpuLnEd_ATgBuWCoeCz_TiJ5vAKabUFnFre_-viRFuuswqHBE2UOPzj3O0aD4AOw3LVeVdmNBPuQtkL6Dc4jP4JrckK9sHfM5KGrgfRHk=)\n[3] [jorgebernhardt.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG78UYUgo-3WildGiNs6JxpVMfAmvC1M77LI1XrDUqYB3WZsT5NOnJqJKTmm_7hVPaaXkXU_5gVOebY5p8QpMA4tNtaTC6no2jWJw_YfW0m6kEEpBr2v