{"step_index":7580,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T17:27:58Z","thinking":"Restore point creation failed, indicating a storage interface incompatibility. The error message explicitly mentions that crash-consistent restore points do not support the current storage interface. Further investigation reveals this incompatibility stems from the Azure VM's NVMe storage, specifically the \"MSFT NVMe Accelerator\" and similar Azure Boost configurations, which are not supported for restore points.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"\\\"az snapshot create\\\" --source --resource-group site:learn.microsoft.com\"","toolAction":"\"Searching az snapshot create syntax\"","toolSummary":"\"Search az snapshot create options\""}}]}
{"step_index":7581,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T17:28:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T17:28:04Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T17:28:07Z\nThe search for \"\"az snapshot create\" --source --resource-group site:learn.microsoft.com\" returned the following summary:\nTo create a snapshot using the Azure CLI, you use the `az snapshot create` command. The `--source` parameter is required to specify the source of the snapshot, which can be a Managed Disk ID, a snapshot ID, or a blob URI[1][2][3].\n\n### Basic Command Syntax\n```bash\naz snapshot create \\\n    --resource-group <resource-group-name> \\\n    --name <snapshot-name> \\\n    --source <source-id-or-uri>\n```\n\n### Key Parameters\n*   **`--resource-group` (`-g`)**: The name of the resource group where the snapshot will be created[1].\n*   **`--name` (`-n`)**: The name of the snapshot[1].\n*   **`--source`**: The identifier of the source. This can be:\n    *   **Managed Disk ID**: Typically retrieved using `az vm show`[2][3].\n    *   **Snapshot ID**: Used when creating an incremental snapshot or copying a snapshot[4][5].\n    *   **Blob URI**: Used when importing from a VHD stored in a storage account[1].\n\n### Common Examples\n\n**1. Create a snapshot from a VM's OS Disk**\nFirst, get the disk ID, then create the snapshot[3]:\n```bash\n# Get the OS disk ID\nosdiskid=$(az vm show -g MyResourceGroup -n MyVM --query \"storageProfile.osDisk.managedDisk.id\" -o tsv)\n\n# Create the snapshot\naz snapshot create -g MyResourceGroup -n MySnapshot --source \"$osdiskid\"\n```\n\n**2. Create an incremental snapshot**\nIncremental snapshots are efficient for backups of managed disks[6].\n```bash\naz snapshot create -g MyResourceGroup -n MySnapshot --source <disk-id> --incremental true\n```\n\n**3. Create a snapshot from a blob URI**\n```bash\naz snapshot create -g MyResourceGroup -n MySnapshot --source https://vhd1234.blob.core.windows.net/vhds/osdisk1234.vhd\n```\n\nFor more details and optional flags (such as `--sku`, `--location`, or `--incremental`), you can refer to the official [az snapshot documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/snapshot?view=azure-cli-latest) on Microsoft Learn[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFnrhVFw3L6RjpteETNJ2skhQgR13hz4eHlXmb6jIgepi1P7OWGkc6MznFlaSd3Hd9Mu5UC788NRg7jzeWcDI89aXSMvu4MKS5eg1Ai8-NkBstD88fJk0z5ZtsAXtNqPKkO5KfZSRTUBqnePrI3uD0xhkjE-_MytDmyC0fNpUW5iw==)\n[2] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH8pF6VDZlfSzOkZSP2AvVPwGvaHEUsrJg_slo8jDtnCU8OnPZeLeFzGiFD_SSOHGXtpcnTxlsdCsQi4Xjt-58O09clnSfB1Ed9fLc66mncOyUd1bhcc3t_qYcEYi-i381A6GtGZwMtP14P5XRl-vYwP393qM_gw8Qch3Pou-VMJUxRB169UBAbbw==)\n[3] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF6bUXltgB84z8_j7UARrScjrIefOrHKIsJeQo0zLUjdkmYSY7rENHU2D0hsjUuTgtBYmalx5QhTp0bJ0fOLGjgqoFg9ldQRKn8M_X6llyuMitrFQbTiFsFYyWZCsmLZq39C3NcQ5qljhSnDNT35qTmX19NSqoEb1zPa5VNo0NEPG__FZRiCzmWpd8=)\n[4] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGi1YDyFwNPdSRQF_pS0PLnw6DwLm7V1pon5gpPEyGal4j9JQXttqcmKr0lDLFR5Y9AbroRLS0xCzDMa7mGpfGfWl_kyNP9LWydQr8fIEYP6fWUhrMGToqtTgd22lfsrpHp5aV3T5tM_OC9eONIk8-YKUxZ92AXWhTYR0u_kfPzBWnF6dk6YjTHjIylIqDoauxejaCDzLoRMKCURkDO)\n[5] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF1uWCQOJ1ywKLQ8Umc-cbPb3wmVRuS2kv76acFxrh-3qH7JxgNDuZzXgm7EEW2dCvzL2K42ump55y2QVcfPYQi4Hkk4i6Gk0WWrUMa5RZQVts7L9mYoNlezSKGCGUWBov4H4QcsPHxMo0rQmdS2eQ15DzDyJeuilpbG3T780Kg9I4-eN_HUPzSTzesqfYBMi6S9CT3-7gfNv8j4fFDZuRpOJs36mXT)\n[6] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEUp1ObxE-aigORXFSA73I3ht3lHlTr0fNLrFWNi0VbwrATu6NJAojjWQOnlHhhMYSDRfIjW_LfRfMcht8QAq4b7iK0A5XSAaFADwMAqTPdhizwT7tlOJG1mt8IEu2AwTdLuvbUVuHvnRdyt9djg9urfen_4Lzlems-_CORwKn2pcPBYOAGWa8hAcQ=)"}
{"step_index":7582,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T17:28:07Z","thinking":"The restore point creation failure stems from an incompatibility. The target virtual machine, utilizing the NVMe Accelerator storage interface, is not supported for crash-consistent restore points by the relevant API. This limitation, according to documentation, restricts compatibility to legacy SCSI disks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"================================================================================\\nAZURE CLOUD SHELL (BASH) - MANAGED DISK SNAPSHOT (NVMe COMPATIBLE)\\n================================================================================\\n\\nWHY SNAPSHOT INSTEAD OF RESTORE POINT?\\nAzure Restore Point API does not support modern NVMe storage interface (Standard_D4ads_v7).\\nThe official Microsoft solution is Managed Disk Snapshot (`az snapshot create`).\\n\\nCOMMAND 1 (Create OS Disk Snapshot):\\naz snapshot create --resource-group FATEHALI_GROUP --name FatehAli_OSDisk_Snapshot_20260925 --source /subscriptions/506deb9a-42fa-468d-b78f-0f25a9e485e1/resourceGroups/FatehAli_group/providers/Microsoft.Compute/disks/FatehAli_OsDisk_1_4a0fe832fe7b45c485920e2a3aaf805a\\n\\n\\nCOMMAND 2 (Verify Snapshot Status):\\naz snapshot show --resource-group FATEHALI_GROUP --name FatehAli_OSDisk_Snapshot_20260925 --query \\\"{Name:name, Status:provisioningState, SizeGB:diskSizeGb, Time:timeCreated}\\\"\\n\\n\\n================================================================================\\nGOOGLE CLOUD SHELL (UBLA ENABLE) COMMAND - EXACT SINGLE-LINE\\n================================================================================\\n\\nCOMMAND 3 (Enable Uniform Bucket-Level Access):\\ngcloud storage buckets update gs://all-vm-backups-vault-irak-2026 --uniform-bucket-level-access\\n\"","Description":"\"Updating command file with az snapshot create for NVMe interface\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/home/azureuser/azure_restore_point_commands.txt\"","toolAction":"\"Updating commands text file\"","toolSummary":"\"Update azure_restore_point_commands.txt with az snapshot create\""}}]}
